# ── Rust / Cargo ──
/target/
debug/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# Cargo.lock is committed on purpose: a security-sensitive crate wants reproducible builds

# ── Python (python/nettls.py — the other half of the §6 contract) ──
# .pyc files are machine-specific (cpython-312, pytest-9.1.1) and were COMMITTED
# here for a while — which put them in `cargo package`, and so into the published
# crate. A crate that commits Cargo.lock for the sake of reproducible builds has
# no business shipping bytecode from one developer's machine in the tarball.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
/python/.venv/

# ── Editor / OS ──
/.idea/
/.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
